      "message": "Correction: my previous reply was incorrect. The Mellanox Adapters PRM, section 3.3.1 (Checksum Offload), states that TX TCP/UDP checksum offload does not require pseudo-header checksum preparation and that the TCP/UDP checksum field is ignored when the device performs the calculation. This direct mlx5 WQE sets the l3cs/l4cs bits, so the generic DPDK offload contract does not apply here. PS46 removes the unnecessary PS45 preparation and restores the PS44 behavior. This also explains why the earlier end-to-end TSO tests passed. PRM: https://network.nvidia.com/files/doc-2020/ethernet-adapters-programming-manual.pdf",
